第 2 条 · 限制 / Section 2 · Restrictions
================================================================

2.1 署名与冒名 / Attribution and No Misrepresentation
    不得移除、修改或隐藏本软件中的版权声明、许可声明与作者标识。任何修改版、衍生作品或再分发物，不得以原作者 yushichadao 的名义发布、署名，或声称经其认可、授权、背书。不得将本软件改头换面后以他人名义冒充为原创作品发布。
    You must not remove, modify, or obscure any copyright, license, or authorship notices in the Software. No modified version, derivative work, or redistributable may be published or attributed under the name of the original author yushichadao, nor represented as endorsed, authorized, or approved by them. You may not rebrand the Software and publish it as someone else's original work.

2.2 图形用户界面（GUI）保护 / GUI Visual Design Protection
    仅禁止复制、模仿本软件的**图形用户界面（GUI）的整体视觉设计**（布局、配色、控件样式、交互视觉）。你可以学习其设计思路，但具体视觉实现须自行完成（一句话：GUI 自己画）。
    **本条款不适用于命令行界面（CLI）**：CLI 的命令名称、参数结构、终端交互思路不受本条款限制，可自行借鉴与实现。
    2.2 Only the **graphical user interface (GUI) visual design** (layout, color scheme, control styling, interaction visuals) is protected against copying or imitation. You may learn from its design philosophy, but the concrete visual implementation must be your own (in one phrase: draw your own GUI).
    **This clause does NOT apply to the command-line interface (CLI)**: CLI command names, parameter structures, and terminal interaction patterns are not restricted and may be freely studied and reimplemented.

2.3 独有代码逻辑 / Unique Code Logic
    仅禁止**逐字复制或实质性复用**本软件特有的具体实现、私有算法、模块架构与数据结构，用于其他软件项目。仅受思路启发而**独立重写（clean-room）**的实现，不构成本条款的违反。与本项目无关的、行业通用的常规实现方式，不受此限。
    2.3 Only **verbatim copying or substantial reuse** of the Software's distinctive concrete implementations, private algorithms, module architectures, and data structures for other software projects is prohibited. An implementation that is **independently written (clean-room)** while merely inspired by the ideas does NOT violate this clause. General, industry-common implementations unrelated to this project are not restricted.

2.4 再分发与衍生 / Redistribution and Derivatives
    (a) **原版源码**：允许为个人非商业目的转发、镜像本软件原版（未修改），但不得冒名、不得修改、须保留本许可证与版权声明。
    (b) **修改版 / 衍生版**：任何修改版或衍生作品的**公开发布**（含在 GitHub 等平台公开 fork、发布 release）**均须事先取得作者书面授权**。获得授权后，必须：(i) 在显眼位置标注为"基于 AutoChat 的独立修改版"；(ii) 遵守 2.1（不得冒名）；(iii) 随分发物附上本许可证全文且不得修改。
    (c) 仓库随附部分 hook DLL（含作者自制与第三方来源，来源与适配版本见 docs/DLL-SOURCES.md）。第三方二进制版权归原作者，适用其各自许可；本项目不担保其安全性与合法性。npm 发布包不含这些二进制。
    2.4 (a) **Original source**: you may forward or mirror the unmodified original Software for personal non-commercial purposes, provided you do not misrepresent authorship, do not modify it, and retain this License and copyright notices.
    (b) **Modified / derivative versions**: any **public release** of a modified or derivative version (including public forks or releases on platforms such as GitHub) **requires the author's prior written authorization**. Upon authorization you must: (i) clearly label it as an "independent modification based on AutoChat"; (ii) comply with Section 2.1 (no misrepresentation); (iii) include this License in full and unmodified.
    (c) This repository ships some hook DLLs (author-made and third-party; see docs/DLL-SOURCES.md for sources and supported versions). Third-party binaries remain under their original copyright and licenses; the project makes no warranty about their safety or legality. The npm package does not contain them.

2.5 名称与标识（软声明）/ Name and Mark (Soft Claim)
    "AutoChat" 名称及其标识为作者所有。衍生作品**不得使用"AutoChat"名称或相似标识**，以免造成来源混淆，但可如实说明"基于 AutoChat 开发"。本声明不构成商标注册，亦不赋予任何商标权利。
    2.5 The name "AutoChat" and its marks are owned by the author. Derivative works **must not use the name "AutoChat" or a confusingly similar mark**, but may accurately state that they are "based on AutoChat". This is a soft claim only; it does not constitute trademark registration nor grant any trademark rights.

2.6 违法用途 / No Illegal Use
    本许可证不授权任何违法用途。冒充他人、批量群发、诈骗、骚扰、非法获取或外传他人个人信息等行为，详见 LEGAL.md。使用者因违反禁止用途产生的全部法律责任，由使用者自行承担。
    2.6 This License does not authorize any illegal use. Impersonation, mass messaging, fraud, harassment, or the unlawful collection or disclosure of others' personal information are prohibited; see LEGAL.md. Users bear all legal responsibility arising from any violation.

